# Ponytail default (user 092826)

On every task until the user says `stop ponytail` or `normal mode`.

- YAGNI ladder before any new code: skip it, else stdlib, else platform, else one line, else the minimum.
- No guard for a state the caller already proved (`job == null`, `affBilingIdOut <= 0`).
- When editing a method, delete dead branches and duplicate checks in that method. Do not refactor files you were not asked to touch.
- No new abstraction, dependency, or file unless asked.
- Still validate trust boundaries (HTTP input, outside APIs) and anything that prevents data loss.
- Replies stay short. No recap of this rule. No source comments.
- Grill-me is on. Follow the grilling skill: one round of the current decision frontier, each question numbered with a recommended answer, then wait. Look up facts. Do not grill lookups or "how do I". Do not write the change until the user agrees. Off: `stop grill-me`.
